          origins: 'Schnapsen is an Austrian two-player form of the wider Sechsundsechzig or Sixty-Six family. It is described as a tightened version of the German game Sechsundsechzig and is closely related to games such as Bauernschnapsen, Talon-Schnapsen, Tute, Tyziacha, and Snapszli.',
